3.2 Relation networks
Relation Networks (RNs) [34] are a neural network architecture designed for reasoning about the relationships between objects. An RN operates on a set of objects O by applying a shared operator to each pair of objects (oi, oj) ∈ O × O. The pairs can be augmented by a global information, and the result of each relational operation is passed through a further global transformation.
